01:00:46.152 --> 01:00:46.340
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

01:00:46.340 --> 01:00:46.940
So how about regulation?

01:00:46.940 --> 01:00:48.710
I mean we, we talk about a free and open

01:00:48.710 --> 01:00:50.440
Internet, but there are certain things
that are going to

01:00:50.440 --> 01:00:53.440
have to be regulated, and if ever there
was something

01:00:54.490 --> 01:00:59.690
that we expect governments and central
banks to control it's currency.

01:00:59.690 --> 01:01:03.300
So how about this impact of this new idea?

01:01:03.300 --> 01:01:07.004
Think a lot of people are obviously
talking about Bitcoin right now

01:01:07.004 --> 01:01:10.641
and it is right to talk about it as
cryptocurrency because Bitcoin

01:01:10.641 --> 01:01:13.680
is just one example of this and while the
focus is on

01:01:13.680 --> 01:01:18.404
cryptocurrency, it's important we talk
about the digital wallets in all of this.

01:01:18.404 --> 01:01:20.513
Because even, let, let's say even if you

01:01:20.513 --> 01:01:23.443
have a regulated cryptocurrency, or an
unregulated one,

01:01:23.443 --> 01:01:26.079
without a digital wallet, it's ultimately
a flawed

01:01:26.079 --> 01:01:28.440
ecosystem and this is what happened in
Canada.

01:01:28.440 --> 01:01:31.710
The Canadians tried to create their own
regulated cryptocurrency

01:01:31.710 --> 01:01:34.340
called Mintchip, which was pegged to the
Canadian dollar.

01:01:34.340 --> 01:01:37.640
But then all the wallets started getting
hacked and people's money got stolen.

01:01:37.640 --> 01:01:40.520
So they, ultimately, decided to, to sunset
it.

01:01:40.520 --> 01:01:44.119
But I think the challenge is, there's
certain, the, the, there's a

01:01:44.119 --> 01:01:48.846
small number of people that wanna engage
in an unregulated, economic system.

01:01:48.846 --> 01:01:52.172
And there's a, there's no shortage of
examples of people that

01:01:52.172 --> 01:01:56.610
have been trying to use BitCoins for money
laundering, for fraud.

01:01:56.610 --> 01:02:00.010
And ultimately, without regulation, a lot
of this is kept in check.

01:02:00.010 --> 01:02:03.516
But the inevitability of cryptocurrency,
is something that

01:02:03.516 --> 01:02:05.650
I think we should all agree, is likely.

01:02:05.650 --> 01:02:08.330
But whether BitCoin is the model, is a
different question.

01:02:08.330 --> 01:02:10.640
&gt;&gt; I should say that the architecture that

01:02:10.640 --> 01:02:14.420
BitCoin represents is of enormous computer
science interest.

01:02:15.490 --> 01:02:20.580
they, the, the gentleman who invented it,
who is now thought to be somebody who

01:02:20.580 --> 01:02:25.630
